    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d702">

                <pb facs="0815" n="805" xml:id="pg805"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">121.67/11–2748: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Smith</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-11-27T13:00:00+03:00">November 27,
                            1948—1 p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 27—1:30 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2751. ReEmbtel 2651.<anchor n="31" xml:id="d702-f1"/> Foreign Office letter dated
                    November 25 states Soviet authorities consider practicable continued travel
                    American diplomatic couriers on Soviet boats to Dairen from Shanghai and
                    therefore regard visit by unarmed naval vessels not necessary.</p>
                <p>In view this reply, believe we should keep this courier route going actively and
                    assign to it selected trained Russian-speaking personnel (as Army guards)
                    capable of exploiting intelligence possibilities.</p>
                <p>Sent Dept 2751; Dept pass Shanghai 39, Dairen 21.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
